  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Extinction (Live at Field of Vision II '26)** (2 other sources): This was the first performance of the song's new metal arrangement; The performance included teases of the songs Head On and Pill [1][3]\n- **Self-Immolate (Live at Field of Vision II '26)** (1 other source): The performance included a dedicated drum solo section during the track [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Stressin' (Live at Field of Vision II '26)**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Smoke & Mirrors (Live at Field of Vision II '26)**: rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Level 5 (Live at Field of Vision II '26)**: rare: 5 archived performances [4]\n- **Rapid Alpha Decay (Live at Field of Vision II '26)**: rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **The Land Before Timeland (Live at Field of Vision II '26)**: rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **kglw2026-08-14.SBD** (recommended): soundboard; 22 songs; 179 min [1]\n- **kglw2026-08-14.mk21.flac24**: source not stated; 22 songs; 179 min [2]\n- **kglw2026-08-14.Thor**: source not stated; 23 songs; 184 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The band introduced the song as being about having a real nice day [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **kglw2026-08-14.SBD**: taped by Sam Joseph, Joseph Santarpia, Gaspard De Meulemeester, Grace Reader and Brandon DeLapp; source: SBD [1]\n- **kglw2026-08-14.mk21.flac24**: taped by Brian Porter; source: Schoeps mk21 (ORTF wide) > kcy > Sonosax SX-M2/LS2 > Sony M10 (24/96) [2]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps mk21 mics, transferred via Sony M10 to 24/96 FLAC [2]\n- **kglw2026-08-14.Thor**: taped by puffanug; transferred by puffanug; source: ADK T7 Thor (ORTF, 9-1/2' high, ~90' from stage, right front corner of FOH, directly in front of stage left array) > PMD661 (Oade concert mod) > 24/96 wav [3]",
